{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The formers of a graven image, all of them are emptiness.</b> They and their idols are emptiness." "<b>And their desired things.</b> That they fashion them with prolongations until they are desirable to the eye, and they are the idols." "<b>And their witnesses, they.</b> For the idols neither see nor know." "<b>That they may be ashamed.</b> Joined with 'and their witnesses, they.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:54.872590432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}